<div class="main">
  <div class="topbar">
    <div class="page-title" id="page-title">Daily funnel table</div>
    <div class="topbar-right">
      <span class="chip danger" id="topChip1">—</span>
      <span class="date-label">as of Aug 15, 2026</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- DAILY -->
  <div class="content active" id="page-daily">
    <div class="insight-banner">
      POS excluded — D2C online only, same filter as your SQL (<code>ORDER_NAME NOT ILIKE '%POS%'</code>). ATC→Order % = orders÷ATC×100. CVR = orders÷sessions×100.
    </div>

    <p class="section-title">CVR trend — last 75 days</p>
    <div class="chart-card full">
      <div class="card-title">Daily CVR (orders ÷ sessions × 100)</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:180px"><canvas id="cvrTrendChart" role="img" aria-label="Daily CVR trend line chart over last 75 days"></canvas></div>
    </div>

    <p class="section-title">Daily consolidated funnel — last 75 days (Shopify, D2C online only, excl. POS)</p>
    <div class="table-legend">
      <span><span class="dot-sq" style="background:var(--bg-danger)"></span>CVR &lt; 0.4% (critical)</span>
      <span><span class="dot-sq" style="background:var(--bg-warning)"></span>CVR 0.4–0.55% (watch)</span>
      <span><span class="dot-sq" style="background:var(--bg-success)"></span>CVR ≥ 0.9% (strong day)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table" id="dailyTable">
        <thead><tr>
          <th>Date</th><th>Sessions</th><th>ATC</th><th title="ATC ÷ sessions × 100">ATC %</th><th>Orders</th><th>Revenue (₹)</th><th>AOV (₹)</th><th title="orders ÷ ATC × 100 — Shopify native, same-system ratio">ATC→Order %</th><th title="orders ÷ sessions × 100">CVR %</th><th title="Today's CVR minus yesterday's CVR, in percentage points">CVR Δ vs prev day</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody id="dailyTableBody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="section-title">Weekly checkout-stage view</p>
    <div class="card-take" style="margin-bottom:10px">GA4 logs 3-15x more "checkout clicks" than Shopify records as actual checkouts — even the more conservative of two GA4 signals shows a real, widening 3-8x gap. Means people are clicking checkout but the server-side record isn't always created.</div>
    <div class="table-scroll" style="max-height:380px">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Week of</th><th>Shopify checkout started</th><th>Shopify orders</th><th title="From magic_checkout_requested per your original file">GA4 Signal 1 (magic_checkout)</th><th title="Ratio of Signal 1 to Shopify checkout started">Ratio 1</th><th title="From GA4_SESSIONS_BY_DATE_SOURCE.CHECKOUTS — likely begin_checkout">GA4 Signal 2 (begin_checkout)</th><th title="Ratio of Signal 2 to Shopify checkout started">Ratio 2</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Aug 10</td><td>3,120</td><td>1,536</td><td>23,533</td><td class="cell-warn">7.5x</td><td>9,699</td><td>3.1x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Aug 3</td><td>3,767</td><td>1,818</td><td>40,584</td><td class="cell-warn">10.8x</td><td>14,110</td><td>3.7x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jul 27</td><td>2,107</td><td>1,124</td><td>30,103</td><td class="cell-neg">14.3x</td><td>9,948</td><td>4.7x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jul 20</td><td>1,870</td><td>1,052</td><td>17,970</td><td>9.6x</td><td>6,347</td><td>3.4x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jul 13</td><td>1,661</td><td>1,164</td><td>19,441</td><td class="cell-warn">11.7x</td><td>6,865</td><td>4.1x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jul 6</td><td>1,553</td><td>1,366</td><td>23,866</td><td class="cell-neg">15.4x</td><td>8,442</td><td class="cell-warn">5.4x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jun 29</td><td>1,632</td><td>1,419</td><td>25,396</td><td class="cell-neg">15.6x</td><td>8,660</td><td class="cell-warn">5.3x</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jun 22</td><td>859</td><td>852</td><td>17,464</td><td class="cell-neg">20.3x</td><td>6,821</td><td class="cell-neg">7.9x</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- HEALTH DASHBOARD -->
  <div class="content" id="page-healthdash">
    <div class="insight-banner">
      Sleepycat sells through the D2C website and physical stores (POS) — shown separately below, and combined in the weekly table further down.
    </div>

    <div class="analyst-note">
      <div class="analyst-head"><div class="analyst-head-left"><div class="analyst-avatar">A</div><div class="analyst-title">Analyst read — today vs yesterday</div></div><span class="roadmap-ref">Roadmap: see "Store parity" P2</span></div>
      <div class="analyst-body" id="todayAnalystBody">Loading…</div>
    </div>

    <p class="section-title">D2C website — today's KPIs</p>
    <div class="kpi-row" id="todayKpiRow"></div>

